        "html": "<article style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:28px;border-radius:26px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#07111f,#164e63,#4338ca);color:white;font-family:system-ui'><small style='letter-spacing:.18em;color:#cffafe'>QUESTION-DRIVEN EXPLANATION</small><h1 style='font:800 31px Georgia;margin:18px 0 10px'>Centralized Zoom Bands + Hysteresis</h1><p style='font-size:16px;color:#dbeafe'>One resolver decides what semantic level the graph is in. Renderers consume the answer instead of inventing their own thresholds.</p><div style='font-size:34px;margin-top:34px'>scale → resolver ↔ hysteresis → band → renderers</div></article>",
