        },
        "title": "Scale Becomes Semantic State",
        "answer": "A zoom band is a named level of semantic detail rather than merely a numeric range. For example: overview, summary, and detail. Scale is continuous, but the interface does not need to reinvent itself at every decimal. The band says what kind of information is appropriate at the current viewing distance.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "Bands turn raw scale into meaningful levels of detail.",
        "notes": "",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786409715166,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
