        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "qa-answer",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/question-driven-explanation-template/classes/nodes/qa-answer.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/question-driven-explanation-template/classes/nodes/qa-answer.node-class.node"
        },
        "title": "Define the Contract First",
        "answer": "Otherwise each renderer change can bake in its own interpretation of zoom before the shared policy exists. Defining the resolver first gives every renderer the same target contract. Rollout then becomes incremental: introduce the resolver, expose the resolved band, and migrate node renderers one at a time without changing what the bands mean.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "Define the semantic contract before teaching renderers to obey it.",
        "notes": "",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786409715166,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
